This was the first ascension I've consciously tried to keep xp level
down to keep monster level down; ascended at level 16. My gnomish
healer started level 1 with a co-aligned altar, and proceeded a
controlled dive to minetown to do the protection racket. While trying
to dilute potions for holy water in a fountain, i lucked into a water
demon wish. (after minetown, about XL 6 or so) I generally hate such
an early wish; preferring to see what parts of my AK naturally present
themselves before burning a wish - decided to go with +2 GDSM. Early
nice equipment included gauntlets of power, a bag of holding, a pair
of gauntlets of dex for when I got some enchant armor. Unable to do
the quest because of lack of reflection (soko had a 2nd bag of
holding), I headed for the castle. A ring of conflict made it easy
down there.

I had decided I would wish for greyswandir and use the likely shield
of reflection from perseus - without a method to break the statue I
brain farted and thought that stone to flesh would make the resulting
perseus have the shield. It did not. Rather than wish for a reflection
method I enchanted some silver dragon scales and switched my mail,
getting into the quest long enough to kill and eat a black dragon,
eliminating much of the risk. used sleep to knock out the clops, then
used the staff or aesculapius to head back down to castle. Cleared it
out with the combo of conflict and the staff, burned a couple wishes
right away on speed boots and a magic marker, having already
identified charging. Grayswandir was next, followed by an oilskin
cloak, and another magic marker. One of the armories held a shield of
reflection, rounding out my armor AK. SDSM, t-shirt, speed boots,
power/dex, oilskin, rounded out by a +2 elven helm. greyswandir
eventually got to +6, staff to +4. a shortage of enchant armor scrolls
and magic markers (had to wish for my only 2) meant my AC wasn't as
high as I'd like it ,especially with relatively low HP (after a nurse
dance, max hp was 185 at it's height.) never got lower than -32. I'm
ok with that if I'm twoweaponing and have tons of HP, but with a
shield I like to be under -40 If I'm going to trade off the offense.

My boy scout's level preparedness AK took a hit when I zapped a wand
of cold at rodney's moat to freeze it only to have no charges left and
when I thought I was aiming my blast I stepped into the water. Many
scrolls blanked, including my gold detections. did find 2 more, but I
wasn't liking how it was looking at this point.

Finally got my ducks in a row, Vlad's being my only "oLS, dropped
rodney with 1 of my 2 wands of death, and headed down to the marked
square. Keeping my level down really did make the sanctum easier, or
so it seemed. Without too much trouble, got the amulet and headed for
home. Mysterious force not too unreasonable, killed Rodney 5 times
total, 4 with /oD.

Didn't have much trouble on the planes, kept conflict going until
astral, the portal on earth was in the first cavern I dug to, switched
back to the Staff of Aesculapius on air and it's healing properties
helped nicely against the elementals, fire was no trouble, and took
off conflict and ascended to Astral.

At this point, all my planning skills took a vacation. I'm not an
astral call bug guy, so I put on my blindfold and looked to see where
I would start. For some odd reason, I made a beeline for Pestilence
(who guarded the western altar). After I got there, I killed him
assisted by liberal use of the unihorn (my /oD out of charges at this
point), I thought better of it and headed for the eastern altar
instead and the easier target of Famine. Checking my pocket for plenty
of royal jelly, I headed for him. Death was nice enough and pop out of
the center chambers to reduce my max hp to 121. Not wanting to take my
chances, I fled, leaving my Angel of Hermes to get walloped. This did
allow me to switch on conflict, which made the going a bit easier.
dropping famine with no problem, by this time my low hp had driven me
to switch to the staff of aesculapius for its regen and healing
invocation. Famine's altar was lawful, so pulling my helm of opposite
alignment from my bag along with about 7 holy waters, I got ready to
make it happen.

OOPS, it's not opposite alignment, it's a cursed -3 helm of
brilliance. I teleport a bunch of crap out of my way, leave Death in
my dust, and head for the center altar. Death smacks me on the way by
and burns up both my 'oLS and my staff's healing. I make it to the
center altar, and breath a sigh of relief as my sacrifice is accepted.
WOOHOO!

I've now ascended an Arc, a priest, a wizard, and now a healer (weird,
I know, starting from the wrong end of the list.) Next up is a Ranger,
a Rogue, a Tourist, or a Monk. Suggestions?


